(PRC-02 — `Create a directory called '<path>'.` performs mkdir(2).
 Also covers: PRC-04 (the article `a` is optional).
 Run from the repo root; the probe creates and removes its own scratch
 directories under this probe directory and leaves nothing behind.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-02.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the article form created the directory
   the article is optional
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_with_article".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_with_article" is available then, print "the article form created the directory".
Create directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_no_article".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_no_article" is available then, print "the article is optional".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_with_article".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_no_article".
